      en: "Usfasgandu is an 18th-century traditional house in Malé, originally built as the residence of the Sultan's vizier (usfaz). The name translates to 'house of the vizier'. It is one of the rare surviving examples of pre-modern Maldivian aristocratic architecture, built from coral stone walls, timber beams, and a thick palm-thatch roof. The interior features intricately carved doors, shutters, and niches. Today, Usfasgandu serves as a museum, displaying period furniture, clothing, and household items. It offers insights into the social hierarchy and craftsmanship of the Maldives before modernization.",
